  "question": {
    "text": "A jar filled with two non mixing liquids 1 and 2 having densities $\\rho_1$ and $\\rho_2$ respectively. A solid ball, made of a material of density $\\rho_3$, is dropped in the jar. It comes to equilibrium in the position shown in the figure. Which of the following is true for $\\rho_1, \\rho_2$ and $\\rho_3$ ?\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/I2hUF8_7m1741ko6Ccu9bHCO5w2oRur3iHggJNxHARg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EQBGo",
      "text": "\n$\\rho_3 < \\rho_1 < \\rho_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "A3JCX",
      "text": "\n$\\rho_1 < \\rho_3 < \\rho_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ILh6n",
      "text": "\n$\\rho_1 < \\rho_2 < \\rho_3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OgVAx",
      "text": "\n$\\rho_1 < \\rho_3 < \\rho_2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As liquid 1 floats above liquid 2 ,\n$$\n\\rho_1 < \\rho_2\n$$\nThe ball is unable to sink into liquid 2 ,\n$\\rho_3 < \\rho_2$ The ball is unable to rise over liquid 1 ,\n$\\begin{array}{ll} & \\rho_1 < \\rho_3 \\\\ \\text { Thus, } & \\rho_1 < \\rho_3 < \\rho_2\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
